A key naming a mapping prints the Swift description of a dictionary:

    [AnyHashable("name"): "Jane Roe"]

FrontmatterCommand.formatValue handles an array one item per line and spells
a null scalar as `null`. Everything else falls through to "\(value)". For a
mapping that is the debug description of a Swift Dictionary, boxed keys and
all, which is not YAML, not TOML, not JSON, and not anything a user can feed
to another tool.

Two things are wrong with it beyond the punctuation. AnyHashable("name")
is an implementation detail of how Yams hands back a mapping and has no
business in output. And Dictionary has no order, so a mapping of more
than one key prints its keys in an order that changes from run to run.

It should print the mapping serialized in the format of the fence, the
same way --format prints a whole fence — for this file, `name: Jane Roe`.
